  "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that <math alttext=\"2 x plus 3 equals 9\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"3 left parenthesis 2 x plus 3 right parenthesis equals 3 left parenthesis 9 right parenthesis\"><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mn>9</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"6 x plus 9 equals 27\"><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn></math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math> from each side of this equation yields <math alttext=\"6 x plus 9 minus 10 equals 27 minus 10\"><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"6 x minus 1 equals 17\"><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></math>. Therefore, the value of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"6 x minus 1\"><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math> is <math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math>.</p>",
